WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.548
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level C one.

2
00:00:05.848 --> 00:00:09.280
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:14.973
Unit thirty-four: Stance Adverbials. Today you will show your attitude to a statement.

4
00:00:15.273 --> 00:00:17.948
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:22.156
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.017 --> 00:00:24.134
Admittedly.

7
00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:27.370
Admittedly means I accept this point.

8
00:00:27.983 --> 00:00:30.099
Admittedly, it is expensive.

9
00:00:30.683 --> 00:00:33.626
Your turn. Say: Admittedly.

10
00:00:36.467 --> 00:00:37.479
Admittedly.

11
00:00:38.217 --> 00:00:39.276
Arguably.

12
00:00:40.283 --> 00:00:42.411
Arguably means a case can be made.

13
00:00:43.017 --> 00:00:44.587
Arguably the best film.

14
00:00:45.183 --> 00:00:47.905
Your turn. Say: Arguably.

15
00:00:50.767 --> 00:00:51.779
Arguably.

16
00:00:52.517 --> 00:00:53.553
Evidently.

17
00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:57.629
Evidently means clearly, as the evidence shows.

18
00:00:58.217 --> 00:00:59.856
Evidently, he was wrong.

19
00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:03.009
Your turn. Say: Evidently.

20
00:01:05.867 --> 00:01:06.914
Evidently.

21
00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:08.907
Undoubtedly.

22
00:01:09.917 --> 00:01:12.125
Undoubtedly means without any doubt.

23
00:01:12.717 --> 00:01:14.879
Undoubtedly, she is talented.

24
00:01:15.483 --> 00:01:18.298
Your turn. Say: Undoubtedly.

25
00:01:21.133 --> 00:01:22.297
Undoubtedly.

26
00:01:23.050 --> 00:01:23.993
Presumably.

27
00:01:24.983 --> 00:01:26.553
Presumably means I assume.

28
00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:28.708
Presumably he is late.

29
00:01:29.317 --> 00:01:31.876
Your turn. Say: Presumably.

30
00:01:34.733 --> 00:01:35.769
Presumably.

31
00:01:36.517 --> 00:01:37.645
Regrettably.

32
00:01:38.650 --> 00:01:40.800
Regrettably means unfortunately.

33
00:01:41.417 --> 00:01:43.474
Regrettably, we must cancel.

34
00:01:44.083 --> 00:01:46.852
Your turn. Say: Regrettably.

35
00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:50.782
Regrettably.

36
00:01:51.517 --> 00:01:52.750
Strictly speaking.

37
00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:56.376
Strictly speaking means in the exact sense.

38
00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:59.192
Strictly speaking, it is not true.

39
00:01:59.783 --> 00:02:03.016
Your turn. Say: Strictly speaking.

40
00:02:05.867 --> 00:02:07.228
Strictly speaking.

41
00:02:07.983 --> 00:02:08.822
Hedge.

42
00:02:09.817 --> 00:02:12.234
Hedge means a word that softens a claim.

43
00:02:12.850 --> 00:02:14.257
Arguably is a hedge.

44
00:02:14.850 --> 00:02:16.713
Your turn. Say: Hedge.

45
00:02:19.567 --> 00:02:20.394
Hedge.

46
00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:25.280
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:26.117 --> 00:02:29.718
Visal, how can I make The plan is good sound more careful?

48
00:02:30.817 --> 00:02:41.317
Add a stance adverbial: Arguably, the plan is good, or Admittedly, the plan is good, though costly. The adverbial shows your attitude to the statement.

49
00:02:42.417 --> 00:02:43.847
What kinds are there?

50
00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:58.927
Certainty: undoubtedly, evidently. Doubt or assumption: presumably, arguably. Attitude: regrettably, fortunately. Limitation: strictly speaking, broadly speaking.

51
00:03:00.017 --> 00:03:01.087
Where do they go?

52
00:03:02.183 --> 00:03:15.252
Usually at the start with a comma, but also before the verb or at the end. In academic writing, hedges like arguably protect you from overclaiming. But too many hedges make a text weak.

53
00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:17.773
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:18.617 --> 00:03:23.345
Grammar focus: Stance adverbial: adverbial plus comma plus clause.

55
00:03:23.645 --> 00:03:24.889
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:25.583 --> 00:03:28.012
Arguably, the plan is the best option.

57
00:03:28.917 --> 00:03:31.079
Regrettably, we must cancel the trip.

58
00:03:31.983 --> 00:03:34.111
Presumably, he is still on his way.

59
00:03:35.067 --> 00:03:42.108
Stance adverbials show certainty, doubt or attitude. Use hedges such as arguably or presumably to avoid overclaiming.

60
00:03:42.850 --> 00:03:46.872
Be careful! Don't say: Arguably, the plan are good.

61
00:03:48.833 --> 00:03:50.984
Say: Arguably, the plan is good.

62
00:03:51.284 --> 00:03:53.086
Keep subject-verb agreement.

63
00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:56.854
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:57.667 --> 00:03:59.167
Showing Where You Stand.

65
00:03:59.467 --> 00:04:02.407
Undoubtedly, the festival was a great success.

66
00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:06.665
Admittedly, tickets were expensive for some families.

67
00:04:07.667 --> 00:04:10.467
Presumably, next year's event will be even bigger.

68
00:04:11.467 --> 00:04:14.174
Regrettably, the weather spoiled the final evening.

69
00:04:15.167 --> 00:04:18.478
Strictly speaking, the festival is not yet finished.

70
00:04:19.567 --> 00:04:23.754
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:24.617 --> 00:04:28.198
blank, the plan is the best option. (a case can be made)

72
00:04:28.498 --> 00:04:32.511
A, Arguably. B, Regrettably. C, Strictly.

73
00:04:36.067 --> 00:04:38.031
The answer is A: Arguably.

74
00:04:39.183 --> 00:04:41.078
Which shows you assume something?

75
00:04:41.378 --> 00:04:45.276
A, Undoubtedly. B, Presumably. C, Evidently.

76
00:04:48.833 --> 00:04:51.123
The answer is B: Presumably.

77
00:04:52.283 --> 00:04:53.981
Which shows sadness?

78
00:04:54.281 --> 00:04:58.027
A, Regrettably. B, Admittedly. C, Arguably.

79
00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:03.543
The answer is A: Regrettably.

80
00:05:04.683 --> 00:05:06.207
A hedge blank a claim.

81
00:05:06.507 --> 00:05:10.462
A, hides. B, softens. C, strengthens.

82
00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:16.058
The answer is B: softens.

83
00:05:17.217 --> 00:05:20.099
According to the reading, what spoiled the final evening?

84
00:05:20.399 --> 00:05:24.156
A, the weather. B, the music. C, the prices.

85
00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:29.560
The answer is A: the weather.

86
00:05:30.767 --> 00:05:33.779
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:34.617 --> 00:05:37.417
Rewrite 'The plan is good' adding a stance adverbial.

88
00:05:46.217 --> 00:05:47.810
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:58.160
Arguably, the plan is good. Admittedly, the plan is good, although it is expensive. The adverbial shows my attitude and makes my claim more careful.

90
00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:00.681
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:01.583 --> 00:06:08.183
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and stance adverbial: adverbial plus comma plus clause.

92
00:06:08.483 --> 00:06:14.073
Today's value is intellectual humility. Admit what you do not know, and stay ready to learn.

93
00:06:14.373 --> 00:06:17.269
See you in Unit thirty-five. Goodbye!

94
00:06:17.569 --> 00:06:20.302
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

